# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# git stores LF, but a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# the working tree to CRLF. docker/init-staging.sh is bind-mounted into a
# Linux container and run by bash, which reads the trailing \r as part of
# each command:
#
#     init-staging.sh: line 7: set: -: invalid option
#     init-staging.sh: line 8: $'\r': command not found
#     init-staging.sh: line 98: syntax error: unexpected end of file
#
# The bench then never starts, and the failure names a line that looks
# fine in an editor. Anything executed inside a container belongs here.
*.sh text eol=lf
